WHERE WE LEFT OFF
-----------------
Active focus: **fonts** — package default + retro so they look the same on every OS.
Non-retro first (make solid on Linux, then Windows); retro polish after.

Font model (round 5):
  • **Non-retro (default):** bundled **Noto Sans 10pt**
      ui/fonts/NotoSans-Regular.ttf
      ui/fonts/NotoSans-Bold.ttf
      ui/fonts/NotoSans-Italic.ttf
      ui/fonts/NotoSans-BoldItalic.ttf
      ui/fonts/LICENSE-NotoSans.txt  (Apache 2.0)
    This is Seifer's Linux system UI font (GNOME/Qt). Bundling it means
    Windows/macOS render the same family/size instead of Segoe UI / SF Pro.
  • **Retro:** bundled **Press Start 2P** only
      ui/fonts/PressStart2P-Regular.ttf + LICENSE-PressStart2P.txt
  • **Terminess:** removed (was unused; mistaken .ui hardcode from earlier).

Retro role sizes (`core/Utils.py` → `FONT_ROLE_SIZES`):
  button  6pt   ← Seifer: width/fit PERFECT — keep
  ui/list 8pt
  table   8pt
  code    9pt
  log    10pt
  about   9pt   (About always forces Press Start even if retro is off)

Non-retro role sizes: all **10pt** Noto Sans (matches this machine).

Retro spacing (looks good per Seifer):
  • List/table/checkbox item padding via QSS (`retroSpacingStylesheet`) —
    never put font-size/padding on QTabBar::tab or general QPushButton chrome
    (Windows native metrics collapse if you do).
  • Log viewer line height ~155% retro / ~125% non-retro.

Log viewer crash FIXED:
  PyQt6: `setLineHeight(height, int)` needs
  `int(QTextBlockFormat.LineHeightTypes.ProportionalHeight.value)`


